I"<p>In the previous post, I explained how to get started with explicit animation in Flutter. In this post, I’ll walk you through how to build a simple animation using all the classes I mentioned. We’re going to make a hand-waving animation using the wave hand emoji.</p>

<h3 id="setting-up-your-project">Setting up your project</h3>

<p>Since the app is intended to only run on Android, I’ll be using the flutter create command to only build the project for Android. Flutter builds a project for some default platforms(Android, IOS, Windows, Linux, Macos, Web); if you want to build for specific platforms, you can specify them using the platforms option.</p>

<p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">flutter create --platforms android wave_hand_app</code></p>

<p>Clean up the default project template in your <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">main.dart</code> file, leaving only the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">main</code> method and the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">stateless widget class</code>. You should have something like this now afte converting your default class to a <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">stateful widget class</code>.</p>

