<p>In the code above, I have a text widget wrapped in a <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">gesture detector</code> that listens for tap events and triggers the animation to start when the event is detected.</p>

<p>The <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">_startWaveAnim</code> method uses the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">repeat</code> method of the animation controller class, which repeats the animation indefinitely. In order to stop the animation after a certain duration, we use a <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">Ticker</code> returned by the repeat method to manually timeout the animation.</p>

